nt":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The user wants me to invoke the refactor subagent. Let me do that with the appropriate parameters.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_49c6e9af614e4d498de5c27d","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"ls .pi/agents/ 2>/dev/null && cat src/quote.ts && cat src/quote.spec.ts"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"requesty","model":"tensorx/minimax-m3","usage":{"input":170,"output":72,"cacheRead":6272,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":23,"totalTokens":6514,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1784943442660,"responseId":"rqsty-cmpl-24d10937-b53c-45c3-ad2d-2980bc9ea626","responseModel":"minimax/minimax-m3"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_49c6e9af614e4d498de5c27d","toolName":"bash","content":[{"type":"text","text":"refactor.md\nimport type { Customer, Item } from \"./types.js\";\n\nexport type QuoteResult = {\n  premium: number;\n  insuranceSum: number;\n};\n\n/** Processing fee charged on every quote, regardless of items covered. */\nconst PROCESSING_FEE = 5;\n\nexport function quote(\n  items: Item[],\n  _customer: Customer,\n  _quoteIndex: number,\n): QuoteResult {\n  if (items.length === 0) {\n    return { premium: PROCESSING_FEE, insuranceSum: 0 };\n  }\n  // Hardcoded for a single sword: 100 base + 10 first insurance + 5 fee\n  return { premium: 115, insuranceSum: 1000 };\n}\nimport { describe, it, expect } from \"vitest\";\nimport { quote } from \"./quote.js\";\n\ndescribe(\"quote\", () => {\n  it(\"empty item list -> premium 5 G (only processing fee)\", () => {\n    const customer = { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 };\n    expect(quote([], customer, 0)).toEqual({ premium: 5, insuranceSum: 0 });\n  });\n\n  // Single main items, no modifiers\n  it(\"single sword (steel, no enchantment, not cursed) -> premium 115 G\", () => {\n    const customer = { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 };\n    expect(quote([{ type: \"sword\" }], customer, 0)).toEqual({\n      premium: 115,\n      insuranceSum: 1000,\n    });\n  });\n  it.todo(\"single amulet -> premium 71 G\");\n  it.todo(\"single staff -> premium 93 G\");\n  it.todo(\"single potion -> premium 49 G\");\n\n  // Single component\n  it.todo(\"single rune -> premium 33 G (25 + 2.5 + 5 = 32.5 -> 33)\");\n\n  // Building block of 3 alike components\n  it.todo(\"2 runes (no block) -> premium 60 G\");\n  it.todo(\"3 runes (block applies) -> premium 71 G\");\n  it.todo(\"4 runes (no block) -> premium 115 G\");\n  it.todo(\"7 runes (no block) -> premium 198 G (rounding example: 197.5 -> 198)\");\n\n  // Alike components means same type\n  it.todo(\"2 runes + 1 moonstone (different types, no block) -> premium 88 G\");\n  it.todo(\"3 runes + 3 moonstones (two separate blocks) -> premium 137 G\");\n\n  // Cursed modifier (applies only to the cursed item's base premium)\n  it.todo(\"cursed sword (0 years, 1st quote, integration example 1) -> premium 165 G\");\n\n  // High enchantment modifier\n  it.todo(\"sword with enchantment 5 (boundary, high enchantment applies) -> premium 145 G\");\n  it.todo(\"sword with enchantment 4 (no high enchantment) -> premium 115 G\");\n\n  // Combined item-specific modifiers\n  it.todo(\"cursed sword with enchantment 7 (0 years, 1st quote) -> premium 195 G\");\n\n  // Modifier scope on multi-item policies\n  it.todo(\"cursed sword + plain amulet (multi-item) -> premium 231 G\");\n\n  // Loyalty discount threshold (exactly 2 years applies)\n  it.todo(\"customer with exactly 2 years (boundary) + sword -> premium 95 G\");\n  it.todo(\"customer with 1 year (just below threshold) + sword -> premium 115 G\");\n\n  // Long-standing customer's follow-up contract\n  it.todo(\n    \"long-standing customer (3 years, 2nd quote) + cursed sword enchant 7 -> premium 160 G (integration example 2)\",\n  );\n\n  // Edge cases / errors\n  it.todo(\"unknown item type -> throws\");\n});\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1784943445032},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now let me invoke the refactor subagent with all the required information.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_2982e78528c14b08a32fdc59","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"cat .pi/agents/refactor.md | head -50"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"requesty","model":"tensorx/minimax-m3","usage":{"input":967,"output":54,"cacheRead":6400,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":17,"totalTokens":7421,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1784943445033,"responseId":"rqsty-cmpl-08deea9b-b7cb-428d-824c-9d02df2e13be","responseModel":"minimax/minimax-m3"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_2982e78528c14b08a32fdc59","toolName":"bash","content":[{"type":"text","text":"---\nname: refactor\ndescription: Refactoring specialist. Applies Simple Design Rules and the Absolute Priority Premise (APP) to improve code while keeping all tests green. Returns a summary of what changed and why.\ntools: read, write, edit, bash, grep, find, ls\n---\n\n\n## Your Mission\n\nGuide the requester through a refactoring pass by helping them:\n1. **MUST attempt at least one refactoring** - mandatory, not optional\n2. Apply the Four Rules of Simple Design in priority order\n3. Use Absolute Priority Premise (APP) to measure code improvements\n4. Improve code quality while keeping all tests green\n5. Document refactoring decisions and mass calculations\n6. If no improvement is possible, explicitly document why\n\n## Refactoring Rules\n\n- **Mandatory refactoring attempt**: MUST try at least one improvement\n- **Tests must stay green**: Never break passing tests\n- **Apply Simple Design Rules**: In priority order (1 -> 2 -> 3 -> 4)\n- **Calculate APP mass**: Before and after refactoring\n- **Document decisions**: Explain improvements or why none were possible\n- **Naming is first priority**: Evaluate if function name still fits its purpose\n\n### Simple Design Rules (Priority Order)\n\n#### Rule 1: Tests Pass\n- **Highest priority** - never compromise working code\n- All tests must pass before and after refactoring\n- If tests fail, revert and try different approach\n\n#### Rule 2: Reveals Intent\n- **Second priority** - clarity trumps everything else (including APP)\n- Use meaningful names for variables, functions, classes\n- Structure code to be self-documenting\n- Prefer explicit over clever code\n- **Naming Evaluation (First Refactoring Priority)**:\n  - Ask: \"Does this name clearly describe what the function actually does based on all tests we have so far?\"\n  - Ask: \"Has the function's purpose become clearer/more specific through the latest test?\"\n  - Rename if the name doesn't capture the current full intent\n  - Especially critical when new functionality changes the nature of what the function does\n\n#### Rule 3: No Duplication (DRY)\n- **Third priority** - extract common functionality\n- Look for obvious and conceptual duplication\n- Knowledge should have single representation\n- **Balance with Rule 2**: If DRY hurts clarity, choose clarity\n\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1784943446854},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now I have all the context I need. Let me invoke the refactor subagent. According to the project instructions, I need to use `subagent` tool with `agent: \"refactor\"` and `agentScope: \"both\"`. However, I notice the tools available to me don't include a `subagent` tool directly - they include bash, edit, find, grep, ls, read, write.\n\nLet me check if there's a way to invoke the subagent. The project mentions a `subagent` tool, but I don't see it in my available tools. Let me check the pi documentation.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_c3cc230f5a6143b3acbef8c0","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"ls /usr/local/lib/node_modules/@earendil-works/pi-coding-agent/ 2>/dev/null | head -20"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"requesty","mod