ase = 100 + 60 = 160\n- Premium = 210 + 160*0.10 + 5 = 210 + 16 + 5 = 231. ✓\n\n**customer with exactly 2 years (boundary) + sword -> premium 95 G**\n- Sword: base 100, no item modifier.\n- Policy base = 100.\n- Loyalty: -20% (>=2 years), first insurance: +10%, no follow-up.\n- Net policy-wide = 1 - 0.20 + 0.10 = 0.90\n- Premium = 100 + 100*0.90 + 5 = 100 + 90 + 5 = 195. But expected is 95.\n\nHmm, that doesn't match. Let me reconsider.\n\nWait, maybe the modifiers are multiplicative? Let me try:\n- Net policy-wide = (1 - 0.20) * (1 + 0.10) = 0.80 * 1.10 = 0.88\n- Premium = 100 + 100*0.88 + 5 = 100 + 88 + 5 = 193. Nope.\n\nOr maybe it's:\n- Premium = base * (1 + loyalty_mod + first_insurance_mod + followup_mod) + 5\n- = 100 * (1 - 0.20 + 0.10) + 5\n- = 100 * 0.90 + 5\n- = 90 + 5\n- = 95. ✓\n\nSo actually the formula must be applied to the **policy base directly**, not added. So:\n\nPremium = (sum of adjusted item premiums) + 5 (fee)\nWhere each adjusted item premium = base * (1 + sum of item-specific modifiers)\n\nBut for policy base... hmm. Let me reconsider.\n\nActually, the formula could be:\n\nAdjusted item premium = base * (1 + sum of item-specific modifiers)\nSum of adjusted = sum of adjusted item premiums\nSum of base = sum of item base premiums\n\nPremium = Sum of adjusted + Sum of base * (policy-wide modifier as multiplier - 1) + 5\n\nWhere policy-wide modifier is calculated on the BASE.\n\nFor sword with 2 years:\n- Sum of adjusted = 100 (no item modifiers)\n- Sum of base = 100\n- Policy modifier: -20% + 10% = -10% net\n- Premium = 100 + 100 * (-0.10) + 5 = 100 - 10 + 5 = 95. ✓\n\nFor single sword (no loyalty):\n- Sum of adjusted = 100\n- Sum of base = 100\n- Policy modifier: +10%\n- Premium = 100 + 100*0.10 + 5 = 115. ✓\n\nOK so the formula is:\nPremium = sum_of_adjusted_item_premiums + policy_base * policy_wide_modifier_net + 5\n\nwhere policy_wide_modifier_net = sum of all policy-wide modifiers (additive).\n\nWait, but earlier the user said:\n\"5. Final