e.isMainItem) {\n    for (const item of group) {\n      adjustedSum += applyMainItemModifiers(item, typeBase.perItemBase);\n    }\n  } else {\n    // Components carry no item-specific modifiers; the type total is the adjusted total.\n    adjustedSum += typeBase.premium;\n  }\n}\n```\n\n**After** (4 lines, one statement per concern):\n```typescript\nfor (const [type, group] of groupByType(items)) {\n  const typeBase = computeTypeBase(type, group.length);\n  policyBase += typeBase.premium;\n  insuranceSum += typeBase.insurance;\n  adjustedSum += computeTypeAdjustedPremium(typeBase, group);\n}\n```\n\n## APP Mass Comparison\n\n**Before** (in main loop body):\n| Component | Count | Mass |\n|-----------|-------|------|\n| Loops (outer + nested) | 2 | 10 |\n| Conditionals | 1 | 4 |\n| Assignments | 5 | 30 |\n| Invocations | 2 | 4 |\n| **Subtotal** | | **48** |\n\n**After** (in main loop body):\n| Component | Count | Mass |\n|-----------|-------|------|\n| Loops | 1 | 5 |\n| Conditionals | 0 | 0 |\n| Assignments | 4 | 24 |\n| Invocations | 2 | 4 |\n| **Subtotal** | | **33** |\n\n**Added** in new helper `computeTypeAdjustedPremium`:\n| Component | Count | Mass |\n|-----------|-------|------|\n| Loops | 1 | 5 |\n| Conditionals | 1 | 4 |\n| Assignments | 2 | 12 |\n| Invocations | 1 | 2 |\n| Bindings (params) | 2 | 2 |\n| **Subtotal** | | **25** |\n\n**Net change**: 33 + 25 = 58 vs. original 48 → **+10 mass**.\n\nThe mass slightly increased because the extracted function adds its own binding/assignment overhead, but **Rule 2 (clarity) trumps APP mass**. The benefits:\n- Main loop is now declarative (\"compute typeBase, add to totals\") rather than mixing level-of-abstraction concerns.\n- The \"main items vs. components\" branching is isolated in one named function.\n- The component-comment moved with the logic it explains.\n- Future per-type premium logic (e.g. enchantment on components) has an obvious home.\n\n## Rules 1, 3, 4 — No Other Improvements Found\n\n- **Rule 1 (Test