eturn when done.","exitCode":0,"messages":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Task: Test file: /home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-25_01-23-55_claim-office-example-mapping_v6.2-with-why-cleaned-pi_minimax-m3-no-thinking/src/quote.spec.ts\nImplementation file: /home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-25_01-23-55_claim-office-example-mapping_v6.2-with-why-cleaned-pi_minimax-m3-no-thinking/src/quote.ts\nPassing tests: 12\nRecent Green phase: The implementation now does real computation. Tests 9 (4 runes), 10 (7 runes), 11 (mixed types no block), 12 (two separate blocks) all passed without code changes.\n\nRefactor the implementation while keeping all tests green.\n\nRun autonomously, return when done."}],"timestamp":1784946020140},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The user is asking me to refactor the implementation. Let me start by reading the test file and implementation file to understand the current state.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_d5180ccaa6574f1c966ab81d","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"/home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-25_01-23-55_claim-office-example-mapping_v6.2-with-why-cleaned-pi_minimax-m3-no-thinking/src/quote.ts"}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_6d7210e3cf90450fa908f776","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"/home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-25_01-23-55_claim-office-example-mapping_v6.2-with-why-cleaned-pi_minimax-m3-no-thinking/src/quote.spec.ts"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"requesty","model":"tensorx/minimax-m3","usage":{"input":170,"output":171,"cacheRead":6272,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":30,"totalTokens":6613,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1784946020160,"responseId":"rqsty-cmpl-95eba1b0-a8ea-424c-b94e-83f2a0e102f7","responseModel":"minimax/minimax-m3"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_d5180ccaa6574f1c966ab81d","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"import type { Customer, Item } from \"./types.js\";\n\nexport type QuoteResult = {\n  premium: number;\n  insuranceSum: number;\n};\n\n/** Flat processing fee charged on every quote, regardless of items covered. */\nconst PROCESSING_FEE = 5;\n\n/** Base premium and insurance sum for a single main (non-component) item of each type. */\nconst MAIN_ITEM_BASES: Record<string, { premium: number; insurance: number }> = {\n  sword: { premium: 100, insurance: 1000 },\n  amulet: { premium: 60, insurance: 600 },\n  staff: { premium: 80, insurance: 800 },\n  potion: { premium: 40, insurance: 400 },\n};\n\n/** Per-item base premium and insurance sum for a component (e.g. rune, moonstone). */\nconst COMPONENT_PREMIUM = 25;\nconst COMPONENT_INSURANCE = 250;\n\n/** Component block rule: when a single type has exactly this many items, charge BLOCK_PREMIUM instead of count * COMPONENT_PREMIUM. */\nconst BLOCK_SIZE = 3;\nconst BLOCK_PREMIUM = 60;\n\n/** Policy-wide modifier rates. They are summed additively into one net modifier applied to the policy base. */\nconst FIRST_INSURANCE_RATE = 0.10;\nconst LOYALTY_DISCOUNT_RATE = 0.20;\nconst LOYALTY_THRESHOLD_YEARS = 2;\nconst FOLLOW_UP_DISCOUNT_RATE = 0.15;\n\n/** Item-specific modifier rates (cursed, high enchantment) applied to a main item's base premium. */\nconst CURSED_RATE = 0.5;\nconst HIGH_ENCHANTMENT_RATE = 0.3;\nconst HIGH_ENCHANTMENT_THRESHOLD = 5;\n\ntype TypeBase = {\n  /** Total base premium for all items of this type (counts the block discount for components). */\n  premium: number;\n  /** Total insurance sum for all items of this type. */\n  insurance: number;\n  /** Per-item base premium, used when applying per-item modifiers to main items. */\n  perItemBase: number;\n  /** True for main items (sword/amulet/staff/potion), false for components. */\n  isMainItem: boolean;\n};\n\n/** Compute totals and per-item base for all items of a single type. Applies the component block rule. */\nfunction computeTypeBase(type: string, count: number): TypeBase {\n  const mainBase = MAIN_ITEM_BASES[type];\n  if (mainBase) {\n    return {\n      premium: mainBase.premium * count,\n      insurance: mainBase.insurance * count,\n      perItemBase: mainBase.premium,\n      isMainItem: true,\n    };\n  }\n  return {\n    premium: count === BLOCK_SIZE ? BLOCK_PREMIUM : COMPONENT_PREMIUM * count,\n    insurance: COMPONENT_INSURANCE * count,\n    perItemBase: COMPONENT_PREMIUM,\n    isMainItem: false,\n  };\n}\n\n/** Apply item-specific modifiers (cursed, high enchantment) to a main item's base premium. Components are never passed here. */\nfunction applyMainItemModifiers(item: Item, basePremium: number): number {\n  let modifier = 0;\n  if (item.cursed) modifier += CURSED_RATE;\n  if (item.enchantment !== undefined && item.enchantment >= HIGH_ENCHANTMENT_THRESHOLD) modifier += HIGH_ENCHANTMENT_RATE;\n  return basePremium * (1 + modifier);\n}\n\n/** Sum the additive policy-wide modifier rates that apply to this customer and quote index. */\nfunction computePolicyModifier(customer: Customer, quoteIndex: number): number {\n  let modifier = FIRST_INSURANCE_RATE;\n  if (customer.yearsWithMHPCO >= LOYALTY_THRESHOLD_YEARS) modifier -= LOYALTY_DISCOUNT_RATE;\n  if (quoteIndex > 0) modifier -= FOLLOW_UP_DISCOUNT_RATE;\n  return modifier;\n}\n\n/** Group items by their type, preserving first-appearance order. */\nfunction groupByType(items: Item[]): Map<string, Item[]> {\n  const groups = new Map<string, Item[]>();\n  for (const item of items) {\n    const existing = groups.get(item.type);\n    if (existing) {\n      existing.push(item);\n    } else {\n      groups.set(item.type, [item]);\n    }\n  }\n  return groups;\n}\n\nexport function quote(\n  items: Item[],\n  customer: Customer,\n  quoteIndex: number,\n): QuoteResult {\n  let policyBase = 0;\n  let insuranceSum = 0;\n  let adjustedSum = 0;\n\n  for (const [type, group] of groupByType(items)) {\n    const typeBase = computeTypeBase(type, group.length);\n    policyBase += typeBase.premium;\n    insuranceSum += typeBase.insurance;\n\n    if (typeBase.isMainItem) {\n      for (const item of group) {\n        adjustedSum += applyMainItemModifiers(item, typeBase.perItemBase);\n      }\n    } else {\n      // Components carry no item-specific modifiers; the type total is the adjusted total.\n      adjustedSum += typeBase.premium;\n    }\n  }\n\n  const policyModifier = computePolicyModifier(customer, quoteIndex);\n  const premium = adjustedSum + policyBase * policyModifier + PROCESSING_FEE;\n\n  return { premium: Math.ceil(premium), insuranceSum };\n}\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1784946024780},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_6d7210e3cf90450fa908f776","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"import { describe, it, expect } from \"vitest\";\nimport { quote } from \"./quote.js\";\n\ndescribe(\"quote\", () => {\n  it(\"empty item list -> premium 5 G (only processing fee)\", () => {\n    const customer = { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 };\n    expect(quote([], customer, 0)).toEqual({ premium: 5, insuranceSum: 0 });\n  });\n\n  // Single main items, no modifiers\n  it(\"single sword (steel, no enchantment, not cursed) -> premium 115 G\", () => {\n    const customer = { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 };\n    expect(quote([{ type: \"sword\" }], customer, 0)).toEqual({\n      premium: 115,\n      insuranceSum: 1000,\n    });\n  });\n  it(\"single amulet -> premium 71 G\", () => {\n    const customer = { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 };\n    expect(quote([{ type: \"amulet\" }], customer, 0)).toEqual({\n      premium: 71,\n      insuranceSum: 600,\n    });\n  });\n  it(\"single staff -> premium 93 G\", () => {\n    const customer = { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 };\n    expect(quote([{ type: \"staff\" }], customer, 0)).toEqual({\n      premium: 93,\n      insuranceSum: 800,\n    });\n  });\n  it(\"single potion -> premium 49 G\", () => {\n    const customer = { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 };\n    expect(quote([{ type: \"potion\" }], customer, 0)).toEqual({\n      premium: 49,\n      insuranceSum: 400,\n    });\n  });\n\n  // Single component\n  it(\"single rune -> premium 33 G (25 + 2.5 + 5 = 32.5 -> 33)\", () => {\n    const customer = { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 };\n    expect(quote([{ type: \"rune\" }], customer, 0)).toEqual({\n      premium: 33,\n      insuranceSum: 250,\n    });\n  });\n\n  // Building block of 3 alike components\n  it(\"2 runes (no block) -> premium 60 G\", () => {\n    const customer = { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 };\n    expect(quote([{ type: \"rune\" }, { type: \"rune\" }], customer, 0)).toEqual({\n      premium: 60,\n      insuranceSum: 500,\n    });\n  });\n  it(\"3 runes (block applies) -> premium 71 G\", () => {\n    const customer = { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 };\n    expect(\n      quote(\n        [{ type: \"rune\" }, { type: \"rune\" }, { type: \"rune\" }],\n        customer,\n        0,\n      ),\n    ).toEqual({\n      premium: 71,\n      insuranceSum: 750,\n    });\n  });\n  it(\"4 runes (no block) -> premium 115 G\", () => {\n    const customer = { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 };\n    const runes = [\n      { type: \"rune\" },\n      { type: \"rune\" },\n      { type: \"rune\" },\n      { type: \"rune\" },\n    ];\n    expect(quote(runes, customer, 0)).toEqual({\n      premium: 115,\n      insuranceSum: 1000,\n    });\n  });\n  it(\"7 runes (no block) -> premium 198 G (rounding example: 197.5 -> 198)\", () => {\n    const customer = { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 };\n    const runes = Array.from({ length: 7 }, () => ({ type: \"rune\" }));\n    expect(quote(runes, customer, 0)).toEqual({\n      premium: 198,\n      insuranceSum: 1750,\n    });\n  });\n\n  // Alike components means same type\n  it(\"2 runes + 1 moonstone (different types, no block) -> premium 88 G\", () => {\n    const customer = { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 };\n    expect(\n      quote(\n        [{ type: \"rune\" }, { type: \"rune\" }, { type: \"moonstone\" }],\n        customer,\n        0,\n      ),\n    ).toEqual({\n      premium: 88,\n      insuranceSum: 750,\n    });\n  });\n  it(\"3 runes + 3 moonstones (two separate blocks) -> premium 137 G\", () => {\n    const customer = { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 };\n    const items = [\n      { type: \"rune\" },\n      { type: \"rune\" },\n      { type: \"rune\" },\n      { type: \"moonstone\" },\n      { type: \"moonstone\" },\n      { type: \"moonstone\" },\n    ];\n    expect(quote(items, customer, 0)).toEqual({\n      premium: 137,\n      insuranceSum: 1500,\n    });\n  });\n\n  // Cursed modifier (applies only to the cursed item's base premium)\n  it.todo(\"cursed sword (0 years, 1st quote, integration example 1) -> premium 165 G\");\n\n  // High enchantment modifier\n  it.todo(\"sword with enchantment 5 (boundary, high enchantment applies) -> premium 145 G\");\n  it.todo(\"sword with enchantment 4 (no high enchantment) -> premium 115 G\");\n\n  // Combined item-specific modifiers\n  it.todo(\"cursed sword with enchantment 7 (0 years, 1st quote) -> premium 195 G\");\n\n  // Modifier scope on multi-item policies\n  it.todo(\"cursed sword + plain amulet (multi-item) -> premium 231 G\");\n\n  // Loyalty discount threshold (exactly 2 years applies)\n  it.todo(\"customer with exactly 2 years (boundary) + sword -> premium 95 G\");\n  it.todo(\"customer with 1 year (just below threshold) + sword -> premium 115 G\");\n\n  // Long-standing customer's follow-up contract\n  it.todo(\n    \"long-standing customer (3 years, 2nd quote) + cursed sword enchant 7 -> premium 160 G (integration example 2)\",\n  );\n\n  // Edge cases / errors\n  it.todo(\"unknown item type -> throws\");\n});\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1784946024780},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Let me understand the current implementation:\n\n1. The `quote` function calculates insurance quotes based on:\n   - Items (with type, cursed flag, enchantment)\n   - Customer info (years with company)\n   - Quote index (for follow-up discount)\n\n2. Current structure:\n   - `PROCESSING_FEE` constant\n   - `MAIN_ITEM_BASES` record for main items (sword, amulet, staff, potion)\n   - `COMPONENT_PREMIUM`, `COMPONENT_INSURANCE` for components (rune, moonstone, etc.)\n   - `BLOCK_SIZE`, `BLOCK_PREMIUM` for component block rule\n   - `FIRST_INSURANCE_RATE`, `LOYALTY_DISCOUNT_RATE`, `LOYALTY_THRESHOLD_YEARS`, `FOLLOW_UP_DISCOUNT_RATE` for policy modifiers\n   - `CURSED_RATE`, `HIGH_ENCHANTMENT_RATE`, `HIGH_ENCHANTMENT_THRESHOLD` for item modifiers\n\n3. Helper functions:\n   - `computeTypeBase(type, count)` - computes totals for a type\n   - `applyMainItemModifiers(item, basePremium)` - applies item-specific modifiers\n   - `computePolicyModifier(customer, quoteIndex)` - computes additive policy modifier\n   - `groupByType(items)` - groups items by type\n\n4. Main `quote` function:\n   - Iterates through groups\n   - Sums policyBase, insuranceSum, adjustedSum\n   - Applies modifiers\n   - Adds processing fee\n   - Ceils the final result\n\nLet me run the tests first to confirm all 12 are passing.\n\nNow let me think about refactoring opportunities. Let me first run the tests to see the baseline.\n\nLooking at the code:\n\n1. **Naming Evaluation**:\n   - `quote` - the function name fits its purpose (calculates a quote)\n   - `computeTypeBase` - reasonable\n   - `applyMainItemModifiers` - clear\n   - `computePolicyModifier` - clear\n   - `groupByType` - clear\n\n2. **Possible Refactorings**:\n   - The main `quote` function has a clear structure already\n   - The `TypeBase` type has 4 fields - might be too much\n   - Looking at the `quote` function, we have `adjustedSum` and `policyBase` - both are computed but actually:\n     - `policyBase += typeBase.premium` (the base premium for all items)\n     - `adjustedSum += adjusted total for type`\n     - For main items, `adjustedSum += applyMainItemModifiers(item, typeBase.perItemBase)` for each\n     - For components, `adjustedSum += typeBase.premium`\n   \n   So `adjustedSum` is actually the sum of all items including the modifier. For components, no modifier is applied so adjustedSum = typeBase.premium. For main items, each item gets its modifiers applied.\n\n   Wait, that's actually subtle. Let me think again:\n   - For a main item with no modifiers: `applyMainItemModifiers` returns `basePremium * 1 = basePremium`\n   - For a main item with cursed: `applyMainItemModifiers` returns `basePremium * 1.5`\n   - For components: `adjustedSum += typeBase.premium` (which is count * COMPONENT_PREMIUM, with block rule)\n\n   So the formula is:\n   - `premium = adjustedSum + policyBase * policyModifier + PROCESSING_FEE`\n   \n   Where:\n   - `policyBase` is the un-modified base premium of all items (used as the basis for the modifier)\n   - `adjustedSum` is the sum after item-specific modifiers are applied (not the policy modifier)\n   - `policyModifier` is applied to `policyBase` (not `adjustedSum`)\n   \n   This is a bit odd. The naming `policyBase` is used for the un-modified sum that gets the policy modifier applied. Let me check this against the tests...\n\n   Actually wait, let me trace through Test 1 (single sword):\n   - sword base premium = 100, insurance = 1000\n   - typeBase = { premium: 100, insurance: 1000, perItemBase: 100, isMainItem: true }\n   - policyBase = 100\n   - insuranceSum = 1000\n   - applyMainItemModifiers({type: \"sword\"}, 100) = 100 * 1 = 100\n   - adjustedSum = 100\n   - policyModifier = 0.10 (FIRST_INSURANCE_RATE)\n   - premium = 100 + 100 * 0.10 + 5 = 115 ✓\n\n   For cursed sword:\n   - applyMainItemModifiers returns 100 * 1.5 = 150\n   - adjustedSum = 150\n   - policyBase = 100\n   - premium = 150 + 100 * 0.10 + 5 = 165 ✓\n\n   OK so the policy modifier is applied to the unmodified base. That's a strange design but I need to keep it because the tests verify this behavior.\n\n   Actually, looking again, this might be intentional. The \"adjustedSum\" accounts for item-level modifiers (cursed, high enchantment), and the \"policyBase\" is the base for the policy-wide modifier (loyalty, follow-up). This separation might be a feature.\n\n3. **DRY Opportunities**:\n   - The `for (const item of group)` loop and the `else { adjustedSum += typeBase.premium; }` branch could be unified.\n   - Actually, for components, we could iterate too and just add the per-item base.\n\n   But wait, components have the BLOCK rule (3 alike = 60 G instead of 75 G), so per-item isn't always COMPONENT_PREMIUM. We can't just iterate and add `perItemBase`.\n\n   Hmm. Let me think.\n\n4. **Simplification opportunities**:\n   - The `TypeBase` type has a `perItemBase` field that's only used when `isMainItem` is true.\n   - The `isMainItem` field is only used to decide whether to apply per-item modifiers.\n   - Could we just always compute per-item base and apply modifiers? Then the block rule for components would need to be applied differently...\n\n   Actually let me think about this more carefully. The block rule is \"3 alike components = 60 G\". So for components, we need to track the block discount. For main items, there's no block rule.\n\n   One approach: For each type, compute the per-item premium. For components, apply the block rule. For main items, the per-item premium is just the type's base. Then iterate items, apply per-item modifiers for main items, and sum.\n\n   But this complicates the block rule logic.\n\n   Alternative: Keep the current structure but simplify.\n\n5. **Other thoughts**:\n   - The `groupByType` function uses imperative code that could be simplified with `Object.groupBy` (but that's ES2024 and may not be available)\n   - Actually, with Map, we need to be careful about insertion order, but the test doesn't seem to care about order\n   - The `quote` function has a `for...of` loop with a nested `for...of` loop\n\nLet me also check the `process.env.PWD` and tests directory structure.\n\nLet me check what's available.\n\nLet me look at the test results first.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_ed0cdc