tems (sword/amulet/staff/potion), false for components. */\n  isMainItem: boolean;\n};\n\n/** Compute totals and per-item base for all items of a single type. Applies the component block rule. */\nfunction computeTypeBase(type: string, count: number): TypeBase {\n\n[77 more lines in file. Use offset=51 to continue.]"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1784946320980},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Let me apply my refactoring. I'll extract `sumAdjustedPremium` from the main loop.\n\nLet me make the edit.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"text","text":"Now I have a clear picture. Let me analyze the code and apply the refactoring.\n\n## Naming Evaluation (FIRST PRIORITY)\n\n- `quote` → clear, fits purpose\n- `computeTypeBase` → clear\n- `applyMainItemModifiers` → clear\n- `computePolicyModifier` → clear\n- `groupByType` → clear\n\nAll names reveal intent well. **Decision: Keep names.**\n\n## Initial APP Mass Analysis (main `quote` function loop body)\n\n```\nfor (const [type, group] of groupByType(items)) {\n  const typeBase = computeTypeBase(type, group.length);\n  policyBase += typeBase.premium;\n  insuranceSum += typeBase.insurance;\n\n  if (typeBase.isMainItem) {\n    for (const item of group) {\n      adjustedSum += applyMainItemModifiers(item, typeBase.perItemBase);\n    }\n  } else {\n    adjustedSum += typeBase.premium;\n  }\n}\n```\n\nComponents counted inside the outer `quote` body:\n- Loops: 2 (outer + nested) = 10\n- Conditionals: 1 = 4\n- Assignments: 5 (typeBase, policyBase, insuranceSum, adjustedSum x2) = 30\n- Invocations: 2 (computeTypeBase, applyMainItemModifiers) = 4\n- **Subtotal for loop body: 48**\n\n## Rule 2 — Reveals Intent\n\nThe nested loop + conditional in the main loop is dense. The \"how do we get the adjusted premium for a type?\" logic is intertwined with the \"sum totals across types\" logic. Extracting this into a named function (`computeTypeAdjustedPremium`) reveals intent better and flattens 