ndings + 1 invocation + 2 conditionals + 0 assignments)\n- **Delta: -13**\n\n**Combined mass reduction: -29**\n\n### Refactoring Applied\n\nBoth `applyMainItemModifiers` and `computePolicyModifier` used a mutation pattern (`let modifier = X; if (...) modifier += Y`). Refactored to declarative style with explanatory bindings:\n\n- `applyMainItemModifiers` now uses `cursedBonus` and `highEnchantmentBonus` named bindings — each conditional's contribution is self-labeled (Rule 2: Reveals Intent).\n- `computePolicyModifier` now uses `loyaltyDiscount` and `followUpDiscount` — the formula `FIRST_INSURANCE_RATE - loyaltyDiscount - followUpDiscount` reads as a definition rather than a sequence of mutations.\n\n### Quality Improvements\n- **Rule 2 (Reveals Intent)**: Each conditional now has a named binding explaining what it computes\n- **Rule 4 (Fewest Elements)**: Eliminated 6 mutation statements across both functions\n- **Immutability**: Functions are now pure expressions; no `let` reassignment\n- **Mass**: Combined reduction of 29 mass units\n\n### Tests\nAll 15 tests pass after refactoring."}],"details":{"mode":"single","agentScope":"both","projectAgentsDir":"/home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-25_01-23-55_claim-office-example-mapping_v6.2-with-why-cleaned-pi_minimax-m3-no-thinking/.pi/agents","results":[{"agent":"refactor","agentSource":"project","task":"Test file: /home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-25_01-23-55_claim-office-example-mapping_v6.2-with-why-cleaned-pi_minimax-m3-no-thinking/src/quote.spec.ts\nImplementation file: /home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-25_01-23-55_claim-office-example-mapping_v6.2-with-why-cleaned-pi_minimax-m3-no-thinking/src/quote.ts\nPassing tests: 15\nRecent Green phase: Tests for cursed sword (165), sword enchant 5 (145), and sword enchant 4 (115) all passed without code changes -- the real implementation correctly handles cursed, high enchantment, and the threshold.\n\nRefactor the implementation while keeping all tests green.\n\nRun autonomously, return when done.","exitCode":0,"messages":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Task: Test file: /home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-25_01-23-55_claim-office-example-mapping_v6.2-with-why-cleaned-pi_minimax-m3-no-thinking/src/quote.spec.ts\nImplementation file: /home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-25_01-23-55_claim-office-example-mapping_v6.2-with-why-cleaned-pi_minimax-m3-no-thinking/src/quote.ts\nPassing tests: 15\nRecent Green phase: Tests for cursed sword (165), sword enchant 5 (145), and sword enchant 4 (115) all passed without code changes -- the real implementation correctly handles cursed, high enchantment, and the threshold.\n\nRefactor the implementation while keeping all tests green.\n\nRun autonomously, return when done."}],"timestamp":1784946464926},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The user is asking me to refactor the implementation. Let me start by reading the current state of the test file and implementation file.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_b558a54936ac4357acc4f7b7","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"/home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-25_01-23-55_claim-office-example-mapping_v6.2-with-why-cleaned-pi_minimax-m3-no-thinking/src/quote.ts"}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_d5779c259be94178bb28e7ca","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"/home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-25_01-23-55_claim-office-example-mapping_v6.2-with-why-cleaned-pi_minimax-m3-no-thinking/src/quote.spec.ts"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"requesty","model":"tensorx/minimax-m3","usage":{"input":172,"output":170,"cacheRead":6272,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":29,"totalTokens":6614,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1784946464946,"responseId":"rqsty-cmpl-5f42eb34-87aa-415b-9616-d866e68fa6cc","responseModel":"minimax/minimax-m3"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_b558a54936ac4357acc4f7b7","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"import type { Customer, Item } from \"./types.js\";\n\nexport type QuoteResult = {\n  premium: number;\n  insuranceSum: number;\n};\n\n/** Flat processing fee charged on every quote, regardless of items covered. */\nconst PROCESSING_FEE = 5;\n\n/** Base premium and insurance sum for a single main (non-component) item of each type. */\nconst MAIN_ITEM_BASES: Record<string, { premium: number; insurance: number }> = {\n  sword: { premium: 100, insurance: 1000 },\n  amulet: { premium: 60, insurance: 600 },\n  staff: { premium: 80, insurance: 800 },\n  potion: { premium: 40, insurance: 400 },\n};\n\n/** Per-item base premium and insurance sum for a component (e.g. rune, moonstone). */\nconst COMPONENT_PREMIUM = 25;\nconst COMPONENT_INSURANCE = 250;\n\n/** Component block rule: when a single type has exactly this many items, charge BLOCK_PREMIUM instead of count * COMPONENT_PREMIUM. */\nconst BLOCK_SIZE = 3;\nconst BLOCK_PREMIUM = 60;\n\n/** Policy-wide modifier rates. They are summed additively into one net modifier applied to the policy base. */\nconst FIRST_INSURANCE_RATE = 0.10;\nconst LOYALTY_DISCOUNT_RATE = 0.20;\nconst LOYALTY_THRESHOLD_YEARS = 2;\nconst FOLLOW_UP_DISCOUNT_RATE = 0.15;\n\n/** Item-specific modifier rates (cursed, high enchantment) applied to a main item's base premium. */\nconst CURSED_RATE = 0.5;\nconst HIGH_ENCHANTMENT_RATE = 0.3;\nconst HIGH_ENCHANTMENT_THRESHOLD = 5;\n\ntype TypeBase = {\n  /** Total base premium for all items of this type (counts the block discount for components). */\n  premium: number;\n  /** Total insurance sum for all items of this type. */\n  insurance: number;\n  /** Per-item base premium, used when applying per-item modifiers to main items. */\n  perItemBase: number;\n  /** True for main items (sword/amulet/staff/potion), false for components. */\n  isMainItem: boolean;\n};\n\n/** Compute totals and per-item base for all items of a single type. Applies the component block rule. */\nfunction computeTypeBase(type: string, count: number): TypeBase {\n  const mainBase = MAIN_ITEM_BASES[type];\n  if (mainBase) {\n    return {\n      premium: mainBase.premium * count,\n      insurance: mainBase.insurance * count,\n      perItemBase: mainBase.premium,\n      isMainItem: true,\n    };\n  }\n  return {\n    premium: count === BLOCK_SIZE ? BLOCK_PREMIUM : COMPONENT_PREMIUM * count,\n    insurance: COMPONENT_INSURANCE * count,\n    perItemBase: COMPONENT_PREMIUM,\n    isMainItem: false,\n  };\n}\n\n/** Apply item-specific modifiers (cursed, high enchantment) to a main item's base premium. Components are never passed here. */\nfunction applyMainItemModifiers(item: Item, basePremium: number): number {\n  let modifier = 0;\n  if (item.cursed) modifier += CURSED_RATE;\n  if (item.enchantment !== undefined && item.enchantment >= HIGH_ENCHANTMENT_THRESHOLD) modifier += HIGH_ENCHANTMENT_RATE;\n  return basePremium * (1 + modifier);\n}\n\n/** Sum the adjusted premium for all items of one type. Main items get per-item modifiers applied; components have no item-specific modifiers, so the type total (already block-adjusted) is used as-is. */\nfunction computeTypeAdjustedPremium(typeBase: TypeBase, group: Item[]): number {\n  if (typeBase.isMainItem) {\n    let sum = 0;\n    for (const item of group) {\n      sum += applyMainItemModifiers(item, typeBase.perItemBase);\n    }\n    return sum;\n  }\n  return typeBase.premium;\n}\n\n/** Sum the additive policy-wide modifier rates that apply to this customer and quote index. */\nfunction computePolicyModifier(customer: Customer, quoteIndex: number): number {\n  let modifier = FIRST_INSURANCE_RATE;\n  if (customer.yearsWithMHPCO >= LOYALTY_THRESHOLD_YEARS) modifier -= LOYALTY_DISCOUNT_RATE;\n  if (quoteIndex > 0) modifier -= FOLLOW_UP_DISCOUNT_RATE;\n  return modifier;\n}\n\n/** Group items by their type, preserving first-appearance order. */\nfunction groupByType(items: Item[]): Map<string, Item[]> {\n  const groups = new Map<string, Item[]>();\n  for (const item of items) {\n    const existing = groups.get(item.type);\n    if (existing) {\n      existing.push(item);\n    } else {\n      groups.set(item.type, [item]);\n    }\n  }\n  return groups;\n}\n\nexport function quote(\n  items: Item[],\n  customer: Customer,\n  quoteIndex: number,\n): QuoteResult {\n  let policyBase = 0;\n  let insuranceSum = 0;\n  let adjustedSum = 0;\n\n  for (const [type, group] of groupByType(items)) {\n    const typeBase = computeTypeBase(type, group.length);\n    policyBase += typeBase.premium;\n    insuranceSum += typeBase.insurance;\n    adjustedSum += computeTypeAdjustedPremium(typeBase, group);\n  }\n\n  const policyModifier = computePolicyModifier(customer, quoteIndex);\n  const premium = adjustedSum + policyBase * policyModifier + PROCESSING_FEE;\n\n  return { premium: Math.ceil(premium), insuranceSum };\n}\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1784946469389},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_d5779c259be94178bb28e7ca","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"import { describe, it, expect } from \"vitest\";\nimport { quote } from \"./quote.js\";\n\ndescribe(\"quote\", () => {\n  it(\"empty item list -> premium 5 G (only processing fee)\", () => {\n    const customer = { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 };\n    expect(quote([], customer, 0)).toEqual({ premium: 5, insuranceSum: 0 });\n  });\n\n  // Single main items, no modifiers\n  it(\"single sword (steel, no enchantment, not cursed) -> premium 115 G\", () => {\n    const customer = { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 };\n    expect(quote([{ type: \"sword\" }], customer, 0)).toEqual({\n      premium: 115,\n      insuranceSum: 1000,\n    });\n  });\n  it(\"single amulet -> premium 71 G\", () => {\n    const customer = { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 };\n    expect(quote([{ type: \"amulet\" }], customer, 0)).toEqual({\n      premium: 71,\n      insuranceSum: 600,\n    });\n  });\n  it(\"single staff -> premium 93 G\", () => {\n    const customer = { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 };\n    expect(quote([{ type: \"staff\" }], customer, 0)).toEqual({\n      premium: 93,\n      insuranceSum: 800,\n    });\n  });\n  it(\"single potion -> premium 49 G\", () => {\n    const customer = { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 };\n    expect(quote([{ type: \"potion\" }], customer, 0)).toEqual({\n      premium: 49,\n      insuranceSum: 400,\n    });\n  });\n\n  // Single component\n  it(\"single rune -> premium 33 G (25 + 2.5 + 5 = 32.5 -> 33)\", () => {\n    const customer = { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 };\n    expect(quote([{ type: \"rune\" }], customer, 0)).toEqual({\n      premium: 33,\n      insuranceSum: 250,\n    });\n  });\n\n  // Building block of 3 alike components\n  it(\"2 runes (no block) -> premium 60 G\", () => {\n    const customer = { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 };\n    expect(quote([{ type: \"rune\" }, { type: \"rune\" }], customer, 0)).toEqual({\n      premium: 60,\n      insuranceSum: 500,\n    });\n  });\n  it(\"3 runes (block applies) -> premium 71 G\", () => {\n    const customer = { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 };\n    expect(\n      quote(\n        [{ type: \"rune\" }, { type: \"rune\" }, { type: \"rune\" }],\n        customer,\n        0,\n      ),\n    ).toEqual({\n      premium: 71,\n      insuranceSum: 750,\n    });\n  });\n  it(\"4 runes (no block) -> premium 115 G\", () => {\n    const customer = { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 };\n    const runes = [\n      { type: \"rune\" },\n      { type: \"rune\" },\n      { type: \"rune\" },\n      { type: \"rune\" },\n    ];\n    expect(quote(runes, customer, 0)).toEqual({\n      premium: 115,\n      insuranceSum: 1000,\n    });\n  });\n  it(\"7 runes (no block) -> premium 198 G (rounding example: 197.5 -> 198)\", () => {\n    const customer = { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 };\n    const runes = Array.from({ length: 7 }, () => ({ type: \"rune\" }));\n    expect(quote(runes, customer, 0)).toEqual({\n      premium: 198,\n      insuranceSum: 1750,\n    });\n  });\n\n  // Alike components means same type\n  it(\"2 runes + 1 moonstone (different types, no block) -> premium 88 G\", () => {\n    const customer = { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 };\n    expect(\n      quote(\n        [{ type: \"rune\" }, { type: \"rune\" }, { type: \"moonstone\" }],\n        customer,\n        0,\n      ),\n    ).toEqual({\n      premium: 88,\n      insuranceSum: 750,\n    });\n  });\n  it(\"3 runes + 3 moonstones (two separate blocks) -> premium 137 G\", () => {\n    const customer = { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 };\n    const items = [\n      { type: \"rune\" },\n      { type: \"rune\" },\n      { type: \"rune\" },\n      { type: \"moonstone\" },\n      { type: \"moonstone\" },\n      { type: \"moonstone\" },\n    ];\n    expect(quote(items, customer, 0)).toEqual({\n      premium: 137,\n      insuranceSum: 1500,\n    });\n  });\n\n  // Cursed modifier (applies only to the cursed item's base premium)\n  it(\"cursed sword (0 years, 1st quote, integration example 1) -> premium 165 G\", () => {\n    const customer = { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 };\n    expect(quote([{ type: \"sword\", cursed: true }], customer, 0)).toEqual({\n      premium: 165,\n      insuranceSum: 1000,\n    });\n  });\n\n  // High enchantment modifier\n  it(\"sword with enchantment 5 (boundary, high enchantment applies) -> premium 145 G\", () => {\n    const customer = { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 };\n    expect(quote([{ type: \"sword\", enchantment: 5 }], customer, 0)).toEqual({\n      premium: 145,\n      insuranceSum: 1000,\n    });\n  });\n  it(\"sword with enchantment 4 (no high enchantment) -> premium 115 G\", () => {\n    const customer = { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 };\n    expect(quote([{ type: \"sword\", enchantment: 4 }], customer, 0)).toEqual({\n      premium: 115,\n      insuranceSum: 1000,\n    });\n  });\n\n  // Combined item-specific modifiers\n  it.todo(\"cursed sword with enchantment 7 (0 years, 1st quote) -> premium 195 G\");\n\n  // Modifier scope on multi-item policies\n  it.todo(\"cursed sword + plain amulet (multi-item) -> premium 231 G\");\n\n  // Loyalty discount threshold (exactly 2 years applies)\n  it.todo(\"customer with exactly 2 years (boundary) + sword -> premium 95 G\");\n  it.todo(\"customer with 1 year (just below threshold) + sword -> premium 115 G\");\n\n  // Long-standing customer's follow-up contract\n  it.todo(\n    \"long-standing customer (3 years, 2nd quote) + cursed sword enchant 7 -> premium 160 G (integration example 2)\",\n  );\n\n  // Edge cases / errors\n  it.todo(\"unknown item type -> throws\");\n});\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1784946469389},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Let me read the types file to understand the data structures being used.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_2a44143d9202400b9c9b89c9","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"/home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-25_01-23-55_claim-office-example-mapping_v6.2-with-why-cleaned-pi_minimax-m3-no-thinking/src/types.ts"}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_0b21800ae4c54e22a6ebe55b","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"ls /home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-25_01-23-55_claim-office-example-mapping_v6.2-with-why-cleaned-pi_minimax-m3-no-thinking/src/"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"requesty","model":"tensorx/minimax-m3","usage":{"input":2871,"output":155,"cacheRead":6528,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":16,"totalTokens":9554,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1784946469389,"responseId":"rqsty-cmpl-757e8254-dbcb-4e7b-a0ad-7dfe62391ea9","responseModel":"minimax/minimax-m3"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_2a44143d9202400b9c9b89c9","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"// Shared types for the MHPCO claim office.\n\nexport type Item = {\n  type: string;\n  material?: string;\n  enchantment?: number;\n  cursed?: boolean;\n};\n\nexport type Customer = {\n  yearsWithMHPCO: number;\n};\n\nexport type Damage = {\n  itemType: string;\n  amount: number;\n};\n\nexport type QuoteStep = {\n  op: \"quote\";\n  items: Item[];\n};\n\nexport type ClaimStep = {\n  op: \"claim\";\n  policy: number;\n  incident: {\n    cause: string;\n    damages: Damage[];\n  };\n};\n\nexport type Step = QuoteStep | ClaimStep;\n\nexport type Scenario = {\n  customer: Customer;\n  steps: Step[];\n};\n\nexport type Policy = {\n  items: Item[];\n  insuranceSum: number;\n  cap: number;\n  remainingCap: number;\n};\n\nexport type QuoteResult = { premium: number };\nexport type ClaimResult = { payout: number; remainingCap: number };\nexport type Result = QuoteResult | ClaimResult;\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1784946473272},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_0b21800ae4c54e22a6ebe55b","toolName":"bash","content":[{"type":"text","text":"claim.spec.ts\nquote.spec.ts\nquote.ts\ntypes.ts\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1784946473272},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now I have a clear understanding of the code. Let me analyze the implementation and run the tests to verify the current state.\n\nLet me first verify the tests pass, then think about refactoring.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_cb40715a62b34024aff2797f","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"pnpm test 2>&1 | tail -30"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"requesty","model":"tensorx/minimax-m3","usage":{"input":328,"output":77,"cacheRead":9472,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":41,"totalTokens":9877,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1784946473272,"responseId":"rqsty-cmpl-595f2741-e9b8-4f0c-8f2c-7b8bd360f5ad","responseModel":"minimax/minimax-m3"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_cb40715a62b34024aff2797f","toolName":"bash","content":[{"type":"text","text":"\n> tdd-experiment-run@ test /home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-25_01-23-55_claim-office-example-mapping_v6.2-with-why-cleaned-pi_minimax-m3-no-thinking\n> vitest run\n\n\n RUN  v1.6.1 /home/experimenter/exp