tation from `quote` into a separate function?\n\nOriginal `quote` body:\n```typescript\nlet policyBase = 0;\nlet insuranceSum = 0;\nlet adjustedSum = 0;\nfor (const [type, group] of groupByType(items)) {\n  const typeBase = computeTypeBase(type, group.length);\n  policyBase += typeBase.premium;\n  insuranceSum += typeBase.insurance;\n  adjustedSum += computeTypeAdjustedPremium(typeBase, group);\n}\nconst policyModifier = computePolicyModifier(customer, quoteIndex);\nconst premium = adjustedSum + policyBase * policyModifier + PROCESSING_FEE;\nreturn { premium: Math.ceil(premium), insuranceSum };\n```\n\nThis is 13 lines (excluding function signature and return). It's pretty cohesive. Extracting into `computePolicyTotals` would reduce `quote` to ~5 lines but add a new function.\n\nLet me go with extracting the loop in `computeTypeAdjustedPremium` as the smaller, less risky refactor.\n\nDecision made. Let me apply it.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"text","text":"I'll perform the refactoring work directly since the subagent tool isn't available in this context, following the refactor agent's process."},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_1fa2a4d441b445b2875b26dd","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"pnpm test 2>&1 | tail -10"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"requesty","model":"tensorx/minimax-m3","usage":{"input":353,"output":22512,"cacheRead":12672,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":22450,"totalTokens":35537,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1784947040766,"responseId":"rqsty-cmpl-600e894c-4963-4232-9052-80d5c7e6cc66","responseModel":"minimax/minimax-m3"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_1fa2a4d441b445b2875b26dd","toolName":"bash","content":[{"type":"text","text":" RUN  v1.6.1 /home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-25_01-23-55_claim-office-example-mapping_v6.2-with-why-cleaned-pi_minimax-m3-no-thinking\n\n ✓ src/quote.spec.ts  (21 tests) 5ms\n ↓ src/claim.spec.ts  (15 test